chapter
  LDL Specification

LDL (Loclass Document Language) is a semantic markup language for technical
documentation.

Its primary goal is to describe the logical structure of a document instead of
its visual representation.

LDL is backend-independent. A renderer is responsible for translating LDL into
a concrete output format such as LaTeX, HTML or DOCX.

When LDL does not yet provide a suitable directive, backend-specific code may
be embedded directly into the document. This code is passed through unchanged
to the corresponding renderer.

section
  Design Principles

LDL describes meaning, not appearance.

